  "title": "Zygris (Zawiet el-Chammas?)",
  "provenance": "Barrington Atlas: BAtlas 73 E2 Zygris",
  "placeTypeURIs": [
    "https://pleiades.stoa.org/vocabularies/place-types/station"
  ],
  "details": "<p>The BAtlDir entries for the two \"Zygris\" labels on Map 73 have exchanged gridsquare numbers. The \"Zygris\" labeled in 72 D2 with a solid \"station\" (diamond) symbol corresponds to the directory entry given the grid square E2 and noting \"Zawiet el-Chammas?\" as the Modern Name / Location.</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "An ancient town of the Zygritai on the ancient Libyan coast. Ptolemy provides the name and coordinates; BAtlDir tentatively associates it with modern Zawiet el-Chammas in Egypt's Matruh governorate.",
